  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220A)=\\frac{2}{3}.$ Notice that relative to $\u2220A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{10x-1}{8x+2} \\\\ 2(8x+2) & =3(10x-1) \\\\ 16x+4 & =30x-3 \\\\ 14x & =7 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =10x-1=10(\\frac{1}{2})-1=4, \\\\ AC & =8x+2=8(\\frac{1}{2})+2=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
